commit 565461b3755f6f91462c4cf28e26080bcb9bda93
Author: liyingli <liyingli@amd.com>
Date:   Wed Oct 21 17:53:15 2026 +0000

    router: --decode-request-weight charges held requests in decode input demand
    
    Under DP attention every decode step waits for the busiest rank, whose cost grows
    with its request count as well as its context. Decode input demand balances
    in-flight input tokens only, so one rank can hold many short requests. The new
    weight (tokens per held request, default 0 = unchanged) adds weight * requests
    to each candidate's projected tokens, the form Dynamo uses for
    router-decode-active-request-weight. Exposes the per-target request count as
    infera_router_decode_demand_requests.
    
    Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
    Signed-off-by: liyingli <liyingli@amd.com>

